## Day 12 – SQL String Functions

### 📌 Overview

Day 12 focuses on SQL String Functions used to manipulate, clean, transform, and format text data. Practical customer and business-oriented examples were used to understand how string functions can support data cleaning and reporting.

### 📚 Topics Covered

* LENGTH()
* UPPER()
* LOWER()
* TRIM()
* LEFT()
* RIGHT()
* SUBSTRING()
* LOCATE()
* REPLACE()
* CONCAT()
* CONCAT_WS()
* REVERSE()
* REPEAT()
* LPAD()
* RPAD()
* Combining multiple string functions
* String-based filtering using LIKE
* Text data cleaning and standardization

### 💼 Practical Analysis

The practice includes customer name formatting, text cleaning, standardizing customer and region values, creating customer identifiers, extracting parts of strings, searching within text, replacing values, and combining multiple text columns.

### ⭐ Important Data Analyst Applications

String functions are commonly used for:

* Cleaning customer names
* Standardizing text data
* Removing unwanted spaces
* Formatting identifiers
* Extracting useful information from text
* Creating reporting fields
* Preparing data for analysis
* Data quality checks

### 🎯 Learning Objective

The objective of Day 12 was to learn how to manipulate and clean text data using SQL String Functions and apply these functions to real-world Data Analyst scenarios.

